<p><a name="footnote9"></a><sup>9</sup>
 Juan Pablo Medina and Juan Marcos  Wlasiuk, <a href="https://www.brookings.edu/wp-content/uploads/2024/09/WP99_Medina-Wlasiuk.pdf">Inflation Dynamics in Latin America:  Lessons from the COVID and Other Episodes</a>, Hutchins Center Working Paper #99, October 2024.</p>
<p><a name="footnote10"></a><sup>10</sup>
 Patrice Robitaille,&nbsp;Tony Zhang,  and Brent Weisberg, &ldquo;<a href="https://www.federalreserve.gov/econres/notes/feds-notes/how-well-anchored-are-long-term-inflation-expectations-in-latin-america-20241220.html">How Well-Anchored  are Long-term Inflation Expectations in Latin America?</a>,&rdquo;  Board of Governors of the Federal Reserve System, December 20, 2024.</p>
<p><a name="footnote11"></a><sup>11</sup>
 Athanasios Orphanides and John C.  Williams, 2005.&nbsp;&ldquo;<a href="https://www.sciencedirect.com/science/article/pii/S1094202505000086">Inflation Scares  and Forecast-Based Monetary Policy</a>,&rdquo;&nbsp;<em>Review of Economic Dynamics</em>,  8(2): 498-527; Anthanasios Orphanides and John C. Williams, 2004. &ldquo;<a href="https://www.nber.org/system/files/chapters/c9559/c9559.pdf">Imperfect Knowledge, Inflation  Expectations, and Monetary Policy</a>,&rdquo;  in&nbsp;<em>The Inflation-Targeting Debate,</em>&nbsp;Ben S. Bernanke and Michael  Woodford (eds.). Chicago: University of Chicago Press for NBER, pp. 201-46;  Athanasios Orphanides and John C. Williams, 2007.&nbsp;&ldquo;<a href="https://www.frbsf.org/economic-research/wp-content/uploads/sites/4/inflation-targeting-under-imperfect-knowledge.pdf">Inflation Targeting  under Imperfect Knowledge</a>,&rdquo;&nbsp;<em>Economic  Review</em>, Federal Reserve Bank of San Francisco, 1-61; Athanasios Orphanides  and John C. Williams, 2013. &ldquo;<a href="https://www.nber.org/books-and-chapters/great-inflation-rebirth-modern-central-banking/monetary-policy-mistakes-and-evolution-inflation-expectations">Monetary Policy Mistakes and the  Evolution of Inflation Expectations</a>,&ldquo; in&nbsp;<em>The Great Inflation: The  Rebirth of Modern Central Banking</em>, ed. by Michael D. Bordo and Athanasios  Orphanides, Chicago: University of Chicago Press, 255-88.</p>
<p><a name="footnote12"></a><sup>12</sup>
